            "result_text": "Perfect! The regex has been successfully created and tested. Here's what the regex does:\n\n## Regex Pattern Breakdown:\n\n**`^(?=.*\\b(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])\\.(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])\\.(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])\\.(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])\\b)`** - Lookahead ensuring an IPv4 address exists on the line\n\n**`.*(\\b\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])\\b)`** - Captures a YYYY-MM-DD date with proper word boundaries\n\n**`(?!.*\\b\\d{4}-(?:0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(?:0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])\\b).*$`** - Negative lookahead ensuring no more dates after the captured one (ensures it's the LAST date)\n\n## Key Features:\n- ✅ **IPv4 Validation**: Matches 0-255 with no leading zeros (octet pattern: `(?:0|[1-9]|[1-9][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])`)\n- ✅ **Date Format**: YYYY-MM-DD with months 01-12 and days 01-31 (Feb 29 allowed for all years)\n- ✅ **Word Boundaries**: `\\b` ensures dates/IPs aren't preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters\n- ✅ **Last Date Only**: Negative lookahead prevents matching if another date exists after it on the same line\n- ✅ **Requires IPv4**: Lookahead ensures the line contains an IPv4 address\n\nThe regex is saved in `/app/regex.txt` and ready to use with Python's `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`."
